      <p><strong>The Stockholm Archipelago</strong> is Sweden's largest archipelago and one of the biggest in the Baltic Sea. Beginning just outside central Stockholm, it stretches more than 80 kilometres eastward and consists of approximately <strong>30,000 islands, islets and rocky skerries</strong>, most of which remain uninhabited.</p>

